WEBVTT

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:23.050
Before I knew it, I abandoned happiness to survive

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:30.190
Lying to myself, I danced clinging on to illusions

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:36.870
At the edge of my vision when I close my eyes

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:42.840
I was searching for your smile

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:50.210
With our memories fading

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:57.290
We hold on to our dreams and run  Yeah

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:04.190
These feelings that I shut away in my heart

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:11.410
I'll now grasp them again

00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:40.850
To restore Kaiba Corporation's reputation, the KC Grand Prix tournament must be a success!

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:44.980
Someone is trying to sabotage me, but it won't work.

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:48.320
I'll catch the culprit!

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:53.900
Chosen duelists, standby to duel!

00:01:55.160 --> 00:02:01.180
Jonouchi vs Mask the Rock

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:51.210
I’m fired up!

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:54.500
Everyone's excited!

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:55.720
Yeah.

00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:59.890
Look.  Jonouchi is pumped up.

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:04.540
What an idiot.

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:08.610
Peace!

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:09.860
Ouch!

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:12.860
Stop it!  It's embarrassing!

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:24.560
That’s...

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:26.300
Mokuba!

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:38.930
Kaiba Corporation presents the KC Grand Prix Tournament to crown the greatest duelist!

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:45.410
The rules are simple.

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:52.710
The duelists chosen from around the world are separated into A and B Blocks.

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:58.680
The one who survives to the end will be the winner of the inaugural KC Grand Prix!

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:08.340
And the winner of the KC Grand Prix earns the right...

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:13.850
...to duel the Battle City champion and Duel King - Yugi Muto!

00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:30.090
Focus your attention on the screen!

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:35.530
I'll now announce the first match in the first round of the tournament!

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:40.020
First, the A Block!

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:43.040
The first match in the first round!

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:44.760
Katsuya Jonouchi!

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:48.470
All right!  It’s great to go first!

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:49.600
Who’s my opponent?

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:53.000
His opponent is Mask the Rock!

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:07.650
When I win the duel, I’ll pull off your mask and reveal your identity!

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:10.000
But it's clear who he is.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:10.960
Yeah.

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:12.440
Yeah.

00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:15.450
B Block's first match in the first round:

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:19.470
Leon Wilson vs Richard Goat!

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:24.540
Leon is also in the first match.

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:27.260
Good luck, Leon!

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:33.690
Later match-ups will be announced after the first matches are completed!

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:41.370
Yugi, say a few words!

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:48.030
Partner, you handle this.

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:52.120
Go up there, Yugi!

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:52.660
C’mon.

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:57.190
Yugi!

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:58.600
What should I do...

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:02.670
They can't see you down there.

00:06:03.490 --> 00:06:05.280
Come up here!

00:06:27.310 --> 00:06:28.680
Kaiba!

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:34.280
Big brother-

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:43.250
Everyone!  I'll say this!

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:46.620
This isn't a festival or a show!

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:50.750
This is a survival game where duelists put their pride on the line!

00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:55.840
You'll see duelists perish!

00:06:55.840 --> 00:07:00.830
And hear only one duelist scream in joy!

00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:03.240
Chosen duelists!

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:07.240
Kaiba Land is now a colosseum!

00:07:07.240 --> 00:07:09.680
Will it be glory or defeat?

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:11.770
If you want to survive, then win!

00:07:11.770 --> 00:07:15.750
Show me how you live!

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:26.840
Kaiba!

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:31.400
That punk always hogs the spotlight!

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:34.770
Where are you, you rat?

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:39.650
I won't let you ruin this tournament.

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:47.690
We'll now begin the first matches of the tournament.

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:53.420
All matches will be held within Kaiba Land, but away from this stadium.

00:07:53.420 --> 00:07:59.420
Only the A and B Block winners will return to this stadium.

00:07:59.420 --> 00:08:03.660
And have a final duel in the center Duel Ring!

00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:08.160
A Block's first match will be held at the Amazon Cruise Zone.

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:13.180
B Block's first match will be at the Water Coaster.

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:17.180
Competitors, go to your designated locations!

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:20.990
Leon!

00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:39.450
Deck.

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:47.500
Sweat.

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:54.280
Leon.

00:08:54.280 --> 00:08:55.300
Y-Yes?

00:08:56.130 --> 00:08:58.780
I won't use anesthesia for today’s operation.

00:08:58.780 --> 00:09:00.780
Uh...  Okay...

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:09.060
Duel!

00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:17.960
It's no accident that they look alike, right?

00:09:17.960 --> 00:09:20.840
It's definitely him.

00:09:22.140 --> 00:09:23.360
Partner.

00:09:26.530 --> 00:09:27.860
Huh?

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:29.850
Where’s Jonouchi?

00:09:32.510 --> 00:09:33.580
Jonouchi!

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:35.030
Jonouchi!

00:09:35.030 --> 00:09:37.630
Hey!  You want one too?

00:09:39.320 --> 00:09:42.500
Jonouchi!  Why are you here?

00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:43.880
Why?

00:09:43.880 --> 00:09:46.350
I have no strength when I’m hungry.

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:48.600
So I'm eating first.

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:52.190
You fool!  The first match has already started!

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:58.950
If you don’t show up within 10 minutes after the start time, you're disqualified!

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:00.650
W-What?!

00:10:00.920 --> 00:10:03.460
I’ll make it in time if I leave now.

00:10:03.460 --> 00:10:05.760
Don’t take the Amazon Cruise lightly.

00:10:05.760 --> 00:10:08.660
It’s a jungle!  You only have 10 minutes!

00:10:09.560 --> 00:10:10.790
This is bad.

00:10:11.620 --> 00:10:14.790
Fine then.  I'll let you-

00:10:15.450 --> 00:10:16.600
Jonouchi?

00:10:16.600 --> 00:10:18.800
Jonouchi!

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:20.080
Wait up!

00:10:20.080 --> 00:10:22.360
You idiot.  I was gonna...

00:10:28.720 --> 00:10:32.130
Land there.  It's the quickest route.

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:35.610
Here I go!

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:46.130
Jonouchi!

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:48.060
Be careful!

00:10:48.670 --> 00:10:50.870
This place has lots of pits!

00:10:50.870 --> 00:10:53.000
Tell me that earlier!

00:11:02.940 --> 00:11:04.190
This way!

00:11:10.420 --> 00:11:12.760
Wasn't that Solid Vision?

00:11:12.760 --> 00:11:13.760
Yeah.

00:11:14.990 --> 00:11:16.020
Damn!

00:11:20.620 --> 00:11:23.630
Ahh!  Stop it!

00:11:23.630 --> 00:11:26.260
C'mon, they're Solid Vision.

00:11:26.260 --> 00:11:28.500
He's the type of guest you want.

00:11:29.970 --> 00:11:31.140
How much time left?

00:11:31.140 --> 00:11:33.100
20 seconds!

00:12:05.440 --> 00:12:06.610
10 seconds left.

00:12:06.610 --> 00:12:08.600
9, 8...

00:12:08.600 --> 00:12:10.610
7, 6...

00:12:10.610 --> 00:12:12.690
5, 4-

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:19.140
I made it, right?

00:12:19.140 --> 00:12:22.150
Huh?  How'd you get here before me?

00:12:22.150 --> 00:12:24.910
There’s a pathway for special guests!

00:12:24.910 --> 00:12:28.130
I tried to tell you about it, but you ran off!

00:12:28.910 --> 00:12:32.890
Say that quicker!  You made me run like mad!

00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:38.900
You made it in time.

00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:40.100
Jonouchi!

00:12:41.040 --> 00:12:42.850
You made it in time!

00:12:42.850 --> 00:12:45.050
That’s why you’re my student-

00:12:45.370 --> 00:12:47.980
I mean, I’ll let you be my student!

00:12:47.980 --> 00:12:51.880
Stop talking nonsense!  Let’s get started!

00:12:51.880 --> 00:12:54.890
Jonouchi doesn’t know who he is?

00:12:54.890 --> 00:12:56.380
Probably not.

00:13:08.660 --> 00:13:10.130
Grandpa...

00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:13.630
So you do know who he is.

00:13:14.130 --> 00:13:15.730
Professor Hopkins!

00:13:16.680 --> 00:13:19.140
Professor, you knew about this?

00:13:19.140 --> 00:13:22.680
I told him that he wouldn’t fool anybody.

00:13:22.680 --> 00:13:25.150
Don’t worry.  No one will find out.

00:13:25.150 --> 00:13:26.780
But still...

00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:30.780
Arthur, I’m sick of staying at home!

00:13:31.260 --> 00:13:34.590
I won’t lose to those youngsters.

00:13:34.590 --> 00:13:38.640
Arthur, I want my moment in the spotlight!

00:13:39.130 --> 00:13:40.250
Sugoroku...

00:13:42.330 --> 00:13:43.800
Grandpa...

00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:47.360
But why does he have to be in disguise?

00:13:47.360 --> 00:13:49.360
Especially one so obvious.

00:13:49.360 --> 00:13:52.420
But it’s not obvious for Jonouchi.

00:13:52.420 --> 00:13:54.440
And he claims to be his student?

00:13:54.440 --> 00:13:57.600
I wonder how Sugoroku duels.

00:13:57.600 --> 00:13:59.520
I’m looking forward to it.

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:00.580
Yeah.

00:14:01.190 --> 00:14:03.150
Grandpa’s strong.

00:14:03.410 --> 00:14:05.450
Is he really?

00:14:05.450 --> 00:14:07.180
You invited him, right?

00:14:07.180 --> 00:14:10.810
No.  He asked me to let him enter.

00:14:12.050 --> 00:14:16.770
He said he taught Yugi how to duel, so I let him enter.

00:14:16.770 --> 00:14:21.590
Come to think of it, I’ve never seen Grandpa duel.

00:14:25.150 --> 00:14:26.950
Here I go, masked man!

00:14:26.950 --> 00:14:27.940
Okay!

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:31.740
Duel!

00:14:33.570 --> 00:14:35.220
I’m going first!

00:14:35.220 --> 00:14:37.700
My turn!  I draw!

00:14:38.090 --> 00:14:41.510
I summon Swordsman of Landstar in attack position!

00:14:42.930 --> 00:14:47.330
I set two cards and end my turn.

00:14:47.580 --> 00:14:49.830
My turn!  I draw!

00:14:50.260 --> 00:14:52.830
I set two cards.

00:14:54.400 --> 00:14:58.350
I summon Wandering Mummy in attack position!

00:15:03.220 --> 00:15:04.750
I end my turn.

00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:07.010
It’s my turn.

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:08.090
I draw!

00:15:08.090 --> 00:15:11.980
I summon Little-Winguard in attack position!

00:15:14.750 --> 00:15:18.800
Swordsman of Landstar attacks Wandering Mummy!

00:15:18.800 --> 00:15:22.600
You fool!  Your monster has less attack points than his!

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:25.300
Be quiet!  I know that!

00:15:25.300 --> 00:15:29.330
I activate my Quick-Play Spell, Graceful Dice!

00:15:30.640 --> 00:15:35.590
My monster’s attack points are multiplied by the number I roll!

00:15:38.890 --> 00:15:41.920
I knew you were going to do that.

00:15:41.920 --> 00:15:44.080
I flip over my set card!

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:47.050
The Continuous Trap, The Legendary Gambler!

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:53.760
What are you doing!

00:15:53.760 --> 00:15:58.340
I can activate this card when you roll a die.

00:15:58.340 --> 00:16:02.780
If I roll a higher number than you, your effect is negated.

00:16:02.780 --> 00:16:03.880
What?

00:16:06.140 --> 00:16:06.870
4!

00:16:09.880 --> 00:16:10.890
6.

00:16:10.890 --> 00:16:12.410
It's not over!

00:16:12.410 --> 00:16:15.380
If I can't be graceful, then I'll use a skull!

00:16:15.800 --> 00:16:21.400
Skull Dice divides your monster’s attack points by the number I roll!

00:16:25.610 --> 00:16:28.700
The Legendary Gambler is a Continuous Trap!

00:16:28.700 --> 00:16:30.370
So I can also roll a die!

00:16:34.460 --> 00:16:35.440
5!

00:16:35.990 --> 00:16:38.420
Take that!  I rolled a 6!

00:16:38.420 --> 00:16:39.570
Damn!

00:16:39.570 --> 00:16:43.580
The battle continues with their original attack points!

00:16:51.560 --> 00:16:55.550
I know everything you’re planning to do!

00:16:57.400 --> 00:17:03.850
Due to Little-Winguard’s effect, it switches to defense position during the End Phase.

00:17:04.660 --> 00:17:06.060
I end my turn.

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:09.070
That's why he’s Jonouchi’s master.

00:17:09.070 --> 00:17:10.080
He's doing well.

00:17:11.060 --> 00:17:12.320
Grandpa...

00:17:12.580 --> 00:17:15.070
My turn!  I draw!

00:17:15.400 --> 00:17:17.440
I flip over my set card!

00:17:17.440 --> 00:17:19.320
Non Aggression Area!

00:17:19.990 --> 00:17:25.040
I activate it by discarding a card during the Standby Phase.

00:17:25.580 --> 00:17:30.600
You can’t Normal Summon or Special Summon during your next turn.

00:17:30.600 --> 00:17:31.560
What?

00:17:31.560 --> 00:17:36.560
I activate the Continuous Spell, Mirage of Nightmare from my hand!

00:17:37.630 --> 00:17:43.160
During your Standby Phase, I can draw until I have four cards in my hand.

00:17:43.160 --> 00:17:48.080
But during my Standby Phase, I have to randomly discard the same amount.

00:17:48.940 --> 00:17:51.300
So this is how Sugoroku duels.

00:17:51.670 --> 00:17:53.590
My other self...

00:17:53.590 --> 00:17:58.730
Impressive.  He’s thinking steps ahead of Jonouchi.

00:17:58.730 --> 00:18:00.020
Yeah.

00:18:00.520 --> 00:18:05.530
But I think Grandpa is planning to do something bigger.

00:18:05.530 --> 00:18:10.530
I set one card and end my turn.

00:18:10.870 --> 00:18:13.040
My turn!  I draw!

00:18:15.670 --> 00:18:16.940
Wait a sec!

00:18:17.840 --> 00:18:25.550
Due to Mirage of Nightmare, I'll draw three cards so that I'll have four cards in my hand.

00:18:25.550 --> 00:18:32.040
But when it's your turn, you have to discard the same number of cards you drew!

00:18:32.560 --> 00:18:33.550
Wrong.

00:18:33.550 --> 00:18:37.060
I flip over my set card, Emergency Provisions!

00:18:37.060 --> 00:18:46.060
By sending a spell or trap card on my field to the graveyard, I regain 1000 life points.

00:18:46.360 --> 00:18:47.600
What?

00:18:48.410 --> 00:18:52.650
I send Mirage of Nightmare to the graveyard!

00:18:53.070 --> 00:18:57.770
Now even if it’s my turn, I don't have to discard any cards.

00:18:58.580 --> 00:19:01.580
Such cheap tricks!

00:19:01.580 --> 00:19:04.100
I’ll crush you in an instant!

00:19:07.100 --> 00:19:11.100
Don’t forget that Non Aggression Area is on the field.

00:19:11.560 --> 00:19:15.420
You’re not allowed to summon a monster this turn.

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:18.850
I know that!  I end my turn!

00:19:18.850 --> 00:19:22.590
It’s my turn.  I draw!

00:19:23.240 --> 00:19:30.320
I activate the Field Spell, Ancient City from my hand!

00:19:38.410 --> 00:19:41.500
What is that?

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:51.710
I tribute Wandering Mummy..

00:19:52.700 --> 00:19:56.320
To summon Ancient Giant in attack position.

00:20:01.460 --> 00:20:07.450
But when this card is faceup, if it doesn’t attack your monster...

00:20:07.450 --> 00:20:11.560
...I take 300 points of damage.

00:20:12.750 --> 00:20:15.700
Grandpa is totally planning to attack!

00:20:16.160 --> 00:20:21.440
I activate the Continuous Spell, Ancient Key from my hand!

00:20:25.440 --> 00:20:32.510
It Special Summons two Stone Giant Tokens in attack position!

00:20:38.510 --> 00:20:47.520
If these Stone Giant Tokens don’t attack your monster, I take 500 points of damage.

00:20:49.220 --> 00:20:53.190
Ancient Giant attacks Little-Winguard!

00:20:58.550 --> 00:21:04.190
Next, my Stone Giant Tokens attack you directly!

00:21:18.870 --> 00:21:21.120
I set one card.

00:21:22.560 --> 00:21:24.190
I end my turn.

00:21:35.870 --> 00:21:37.070
Grandpa...

00:21:40.900 --> 00:21:42.010
Damn!

00:21:58.640 --> 00:22:07.520
The streets flow by, colored in red

00:22:08.050 --> 00:22:15.890
If you notice your pain, it changes to joy

00:22:17.620 --> 00:22:27.050
People learn of friendship every time they wipe their tears

00:22:27.660 --> 00:22:36.540
With the warm strength you gave me, I'll change them into kindness

00:22:37.140 --> 00:22:45.600
My overflowing emotions don't stop

00:22:46.380 --> 00:22:51.110
I'll live feeling them

00:22:51.720 --> 00:22:56.260
For me to be me

00:22:56.260 --> 00:23:04.750
Overflowing friendship heals me

00:23:05.430 --> 00:23:10.390
Our chance meeting was real

00:23:10.910 --> 00:23:20.050
We'll both understand that someday

00:23:26.820 --> 00:23:33.750
Sugoroku-  I mean Mask the Rock's skillful strategy flusters Jonouchi.

00:23:33.750 --> 00:23:38.050
As his master, he knows Jonouchi's strategies.

00:23:38.050 --> 00:23:42.110
Jonouchi is rattled and forgets how to duel his own duel.

00:23:42.110 --> 00:23:44.690
Calm down!  This isn't like you!

00:23:44.690 --> 00:23:47.040
You have to enjoy dueling!

00:23:47.040 --> 00:23:50.410
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
The Illusory Ancient Dragon

00:23:50.410 --> 00:23:52.030
Duel, standby!
